    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="1035" n="1023" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1023"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to Mr. Walter S. Robertson, at
                        Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-11">11 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>866. Please contact Doctor Leighton Stuart<anchor n="51" xml:id="d532-f1"/> of
                    Yenching University and see if he would be willing to come to Nanking for a week
                    or 10 days, to assist me quietly by influencing certain Chinese officials of his
                    acquaintance to a more moderate or tolerant point of view during current
                    negotiations.</p>
                <p>I am requesting such services of several others: Frank Price,<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d532-f2"/> Doctor Wu Yi-fang of Ginling College, General Li<anchor
                        n="53" xml:id="d532-f3"/> of Army Medical Corps. W. P. Mills<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d532-f4"/> suggested Dr. Stuart’s name. I would provide
                    transportation. Arrival here would have to be during next 5 days.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d532-f1" n="51" xml:id="d532-f1-content">
                <p>American President of Yenching University, Peiping.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d532-f2" n="52" xml:id="d532-f2-content">
                <p>Dr. Price had been American adviser to President Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d532-f3" n="53" xml:id="d532-f3-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Chen-pien Li, M. D., Director of the Serum Institute of the Chinese
                    Ministry of War.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d532-f4" n="54" xml:id="d532-f4-content">
                <p>Dr. Mills was head of the American missionary group at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
